aw882xx: per-stream progress messages to debug level (y700 DRAFT, NOT APPLIED, 2026-10-16)

Every time the speaker PCM opens and closes, the vendor driver logs about 20 lines per amplifier at
info level on the way up (startup "playback enter", hw_params, "mute state=0", startup work, start_pa
"enter", reg_update/pwd/amppd/dither/pll/sysst/uls_hmute/mute/int/intmask/monitor "done"/"enter") and
about 10 on the way down, i.e. ~60 kernel log lines for the two amplifiers per sound after silence
(SUSPEND.md 5.4). They say nothing that the outcome lines do not: keep "start success" (the README's
evidence that both amplifiers started) and every aw_dev_err ("pll&clk check fail", "start failed",
"check fail"), and turn the 33 progress messages into aw_dev_dbg (pr_debug: compiled away without
CONFIG_DYNAMIC_DEBUG, switchable at run time with it). Probe-time info messages are not touched.
No functional change: only the printk level of messages, no register access, no control flow.

Against joonhoekim/tb323fu-linux kernel/out-of-tree/aw882xx at 0c7c0c4 = helper-v0.4.2 (the four files
have the same blob ids in both). Applies with `git -C <tb323fu-linux> apply` or `patch -p1` from the
tree root. Re-enable at run time (if CONFIG_DYNAMIC_DEBUG=y):
  echo 'module snd_soc_aw882xx +p' > /sys/kernel/debug/dynamic_debug/control

